                <pb facs="0326" n="198" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg198"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 146.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cheng Tsao Ju to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chinese Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington, D.
                                C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1885-11-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 9, 1885</date>. (Received
                        Nov. 9.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 7th instant, inclosing two copies of the President’s
                    proclamation providing for the protection of the Chinese residents of Washington
                    Territory.</p>
                <p>I take pleasure in expressing to you, Mr. Secretary, my profound thanks for the
                    prompt efforts of the Government of the United States in suppressing the lawless
                    combinations against the welfare and peace of the Chinese in that Territory.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>CHENG TSAO JU.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
